special_abilities:
  - name: "Secret Resources: Suppliers"
    description: "Starts with four suppliers: people who quietly provide disguises, special glues and paints, clothing and gear with concealed compartments, false teeth and facial appliances, miniaturized smoke and stink bombs, listening devices, modified weapons and contraband. Most are criminals or outcasts serving the underworld, others honest craftsmen, smiths, tailors and Operators glad of commissioned work; most neither know nor ask the agent''s profession, and all work for money or a trade of goods or services. They are the Smoke Soldier''s own and unknown to the Warlord or his Knights. More are made through role-playing."
  - name: "Secret Resources: Special Contacts"
    description: "Starts with two special contacts: smugglers, trusted couriers, weapons dealers, fences, forgers, thieves, mercenaries, keepers of safe houses, doctors who treat injuries without asking questions and the like, D-Bees and practitioners of magic included. They work for money, trade, a favor, revenge or patriotism, are never completely trusted and may have an agenda of their own. More are made through role-playing and interaction with NPCs."
  - name: "Secret Resources: Snitches and Informants"
    description: "Professional informants moved by money, revenge, influence, business or blackmail, who meet at places where they feel safe or communicate by secret code. They are anarchist or evil, can be bought or threatened by anyone, raise their price when they smell desperation, sell the same information to the agent''s enemies, lead agents into ambushes if the price is right, and will sell whatever the spy lets slip, including the fact of his visit and what he asked. The book prints no starting number."
  - name: "Hide-Out"
    description: "Starts with one sanctuary: a safe basement, a room at a boarding house or a home in some village, likely holding ready-to-use disguises, wigs, gimmick clothing and perhaps a complete make-up room and lab. A player character can establish others; an NPC has one or two per level of experience."
