extraction_notes: "WB17 Warlords of Russia printed 89-91 (cache p090-p092, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer. The entry starts at the heading on cache p090 line 7 and ends with its Money and Cybernetics lines on cache p092 lines 46-58, past two page breaks. || HEADING: Soldati Dimiye / Smoke Soldiers - Warlord Agent O.C.C.; the stat block is headed The Smoke Soldier/Spy O.C.C. Listed under Warlord Troops and Men at Arms O.C.C.s on printed 57, so men_of_arms is true and occ_group is men-of-arms. || XP: the ladder for the Smoke Soldier on the Experience Tables, printed 6, read off a render and taken from the brief. || BONUSES: +1 action/attack per melee stored flat; +1 initiative at levels 1, 3, 5, 8, 11, 13 and 15, +1 disarm at 2, 6, 10 and 13, +1 save vs Horror Factor at 1, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9, 12 and 15; the level-1 steps are in bonuses and the rest in at_level, as printed. || Speaks Russian at 98% is stored as Language: Russian base 98 with per_level 0, a flat printed percentage. Surveillance Systems is the catalog''s Surveillance; TV/Video is T.V./Video; Imitate Voices and Impersonation is Imitate Voices & Sounds; Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic. Martial Arts or Assassin (pick one) is a one-of-two choice with no price and no alignment condition printed, so there is no hand_to_hand block. One ancient W.P. and one W.P. of any kind are category picks with the limit in the note. || RELATED: the Pilot line excepts Power Armor and Robot, stored as the Robots & Power Armor row and every Robot Combat row; the catalog''s Air Assault Armor and Combat Pod rows are NOT excepted because the entry does not name them - a reviewer should decide. Electrical Basic only is Basic Electronics; Mechanical Basic and automotive only is Basic Mechanics and Automotive Mechanics; Science Math only is the two Mathematics rows. At least one related skill from Espionage is stored as a minimum of 1 against the level-one count of 4; the sentence could also be read as one per later pair of picks, which the draft does not enforce. || PSIONICS: the entry grants none (30% of Smoke Soldiers have some; the prose names Total Recall, Sixth Sense and Presence Sense as typical), so no block. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits stored (the text layer prints !D6xlOOO); the salary of about 2000 credits a month and the right to keep booty are in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT readings: light body armor is the generic light-mdc-body-armor row; heavy body armor is battleforge-body-armor, the heavy suit this book prints, though the entry names no model; silver dagger is knife-silver-plated; silver cross and chain is small-silver-cross; small mallet is hammer-and-mallet; hand-held flares are triax-handheld-flare (name Handheld Flare); hand-held video camera is video-camera-digital-mini; pocket disk recorder is pocket-digital-disc-recorder; sketchbook is the soft-cover sketch book row; markers and pens are the marker row. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: one energy rifle of choice, two energy pistols of choice and one other weapon of choice (usually a Vibro-Whip, Vibro-Blade or something concealable); a grappling hook and 60 feet of thin nylon cord (600 lb test; the catalog''s hook row is a hook WITH 100 feet of line and its cord row is a 50 foot bundle); four pairs of everyday clothing; a long winter coat or cloak; two pairs of disguise clothing; a disguise kit with make-up, glue, 1D4+2 hair dyes, body paint and basic appliances; the motorcycle (the catalog holds only named models); the hide-out. Equipment Available On Assignment is prose in GM Notes. || CONTACTS: four suppliers and two special contacts to start are special_abilities prose; the book prints no number for snitches."
---

## Lore

The Soldati Dimiye are a Warlord''s master spies: part commando, part secret
agent, part shadow. A War Camp of tens of thousands may hold no more than
fifty to a hundred of them. They gather intelligence, infiltrate rivals,
carry secret messages, steal, sabotage, rescue, kidnap and kill, and they do
it behind faces that are rarely their own.

What sets them apart is attention. A Smoke Soldier watches without seeming
to, remembers what was seen, and reads meaning into who is absent, who is
keeping company with whom, and what a nervous voice gives away. What an
enemy loves, hates or fears is treated as a tool to be used against him.

They stand unusually high in the command structure, often answering to the
Warlord himself, and most of their identities are kept secret even inside
their own Camp. The Warlords cultivate that uncertainty on purpose: nobody
can be sure the officer, the friend or the grinning Reaver beside him is
not one of them.

## GM Notes

Contacts at creation: four suppliers and two special contacts, plus whatever
informants the GM allows (the book gives no number for snitches). None of
them are known to the Warlord, and none are completely trustworthy;
informants in particular will sell the agent out for the right price.

One hide-out to start. It probably holds extra disguises, wigs, costumes and
gimmick clothing, and may hold a full make-up room and lab. NPC Smoke
Soldiers have one or two hide-outs per level.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one energy rifle of choice, two
energy pistols of choice, one other weapon of choice (usually a Vibro-Whip,
Vibro-Blade or something concealable); a grappling hook and 60 feet of thin
nylon cord (600 lb test); four pairs of everyday clothing, a long winter
coat or cloak, two pairs of disguise clothing (accurate and current as of
the start of play) and a disguise kit with make-up, glue, 1D4+2 hair dyes,
body paint and basic appliances. The survival knife may instead be another
small ancient weapon. The heavy armor on the sheet is a reading: the book
says only a suit of heavy body armor.

Vehicles: every Smoke Soldier owns a bicycle, a motorcycle and a hovercycle
(the motorcycle is not on the sheet). Others may be had through the Warlord.

Money is 1D6x1000 credits. Salary is about 2000 credits a month, and the
agent may usually keep booty stolen on the job as long as it does not
endanger the mission.

On assignment the Warlord may furnish almost anything: Fusion Blocks and
other explosives, special weapons and vehicles, disguises, medals, false
papers, and money, gold or gems for payment and bribes.

Psionics are not part of the class, but 30% of Smoke Soldiers have them
(19% Minor, 10% Major, 1% Master). Among the rest, about one third carry
2-8 implants or one bionic limb and 2-4 implants.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'smoke-soldier');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'smoke-soldier';

